    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d575">

                <pb facs="0737" n="645" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v01/pg645"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 800.852/90</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Morris</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-04-27T21:00:00+09:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 27, 1918, 9 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received April 28, 5.47 a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>No. 13. Supplementing my serial No. 3<anchor n="1" xml:id="d575-f1"/>. All
                    charters formally executed. Certified copies being sent by pouch. <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Shakano-o</hi> leaves May 20 for Seattle; <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Kunajiri</hi> leaves in May for Tacoma; all others as
                    previously reported in my No. 3. No chartered ships will be delivered at
                    Japanese ports.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Morris</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d575-f1" n="1" xml:id="d575-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; gives sailing dates and destinations of 23 chartered ships totaling
                    151,266 tons.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
